y="The table has 3 columns and 14 rows. The first row is a header row with entries “System”, “Static Friction mu sub s”, and “Kinetic Friction mu sub k”. The second row has entries Rubber on dry concrete, 1.0, and 0.7. The third row has entries Rubber on wet concrete, 0.5-0.7, and 0.3-0.5. The fourth row has entries Wood on wood,  0.5, 0.3. The fifth row has entries Waxed wood on wet snow,  0.14, and 0.1. The sixth row has entries Metal on wood,  0.5, and 0.3. The seventh row has entries Steel on steel (dry), 0.6, and 0.3. The eight row has entries Steel on steel (oiled), 0.05, and 0.03. The ninth row has entries Teflon on steel, 0.04, and 0.04. The tenth row has entries Bone lubricated by synovial fluid, 0.016, and 0.015. The eleventh row has entries Shoes on wood, 0.9, and 0.7. The twelfth row has entries Shoes on ice, 0.1, and 0.05. The thirteenth row has entries Ice on ice, 0.1, and 0.03. The fourteenth row has entries Steel on ice, 0.4, and 0.02."><thead>
